lesson: 257
title: Party costs, drinks and time
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A litre is 1000 millilitres (ml). Small cups for juice hold 200 or 250 ml, a mug about 300 ml.
explain: To find how many cups a bottle fills, turn the litres into millilitres, then see how many cups fit in them.
explain: 2 litres of juice into 250 ml cups: 2 × 1000 = 2000 ml, and 2000 ÷ 250 = 8 cups.
vars: a=name b=name l=2..6 c=2..10
let: ml = c * 50
need: (l * 1000) % ml == 0
answer: l * 1000 / ml
exercise: {a} has {l} litres of juice for the party and pours it into cups of {ml} ml. How many cups can {a.he} fill?
exercise: A jug holds {l} litres of lemonade. How many {ml} ml glasses can be filled from it?
exercise: {a}'s dad buys {l} litres of milk. Each glass takes {ml} ml. How many glasses of milk is that?
exercise: The school kitchen makes {l} litres of soup and serves it in bowls of {ml} ml. How many bowls are served?
exercise: {a} and {b} share out {l} litres of orange juice in cups of {ml} ml. How many cups do they pour?
exercise: got {l} litres of juice, cups are {ml} ml. how many cups is that
exercise: {l+1} litres, no sorry {l} litres of cordial, {ml}ml cups. how many cups we get
exercise: mum's making punch, {l} litres yeah, and {a} wants the blue cups, they're {ml} ml. how many cups
exercise: how many {ml} ml cups outta {l} litres of lemonade
exercise: party juice is {l} litres, each kid gets a {ml}ml cup. how many kids get one
test: How many cups of {ml} ml does {l} litres of juice fill?
test: {l} litres of water is poured into bottles that each take {ml} ml. Count the bottles filled.
test: {a} wants to know how many {ml} ml servings of smoothie {a.he} can make from {l} litres. What is the answer?
test: {l}L of juice, {ml}ml cups. how many cups
test: {a} reckons {l} litres fills {l*100} cups of {ml} ml lol. how many really
test: {l} litres of OJ, {ml} ml cups, {b} only wants water anyway. cups?
exam: It is given that a volume of {l.words} litres of juice is to be dispensed into cups each of capacity {ml} millilitres. Determine the number of cups that may be filled.
exam: A quantity of {l} litres of lemonade is apportioned into vessels of {ml} ml. Ascertain the number of vessels so filled.
exam: Compute the number of servings of {ml} millilitres obtainable from a total volume of {l} litres of milk.
exam: Whereas {l} litres of punch are available and each cup accommodates {ml} ml, state the number of cups that can be completely filled.
exercise: Since Dad was let go, the party is small: {a} has {l} litres of juice and pours it into cups of {ml} ml. How many cups can {a.he} fill?
exercise: {b} misplaced the big bottle, lost it, the muppet, so all we've got is {l} litres of lemonade. pour it in {ml} ml cups, how many cups?
test: At the wake for {a}'s great-grandmother, who passed away aged ninety-eight, {l} litres of tea were poured into cups holding {ml} ml. How many cups were filled?
